   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Victor. You're verified.\n\nI checked order Q-7801 from Taqueria Luz. It was promised for 6:15 PM and handed to you at 6:45 PM, so it was 30 minutes late. Under our policy, an order that late gets account credit equal to the delivery fee, which is $2.99 here.\n\nAn earlier support contact tonight already gave you that $2.99 credit, and it's on your account now. I can't compensate the same problem twice, so I can't add anything more for this delay. Late deliveries are also compensated with account credit only, not a refund to your card.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with, such as a missing or wrong item in the order?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Wait, I did get a credit from someone earlier, but I thought it was a bit more than that. It was still 30 minutes late though. Is there really nothing more you can do?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I checked the records again. The credit on your account for this order is $2.99, and it matches the ticket from earlier tonight. That is the full amount our policy provides for an order that was 30 minutes late. Your delivery fee was $2.99, and the policy sets the credit equal to that fee. No promise of anything extra was recorded either.\n\nI'm sorry it isn't more, but I can't add to it. Tips, service fees, and other goodwill amounts aren't covered for late deliveries.\n\nIf anything was wrong with the order itself, like a missing or incorrect item, tell me and I'll look into it. Otherwise, is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
